    {
      "id": 56401,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-03-25T18:28:10.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Isolated hero isn't the worst clue card to get. The only heroes it will always be bad to attach itself to is Legacy and Argent. Everyone else is just fine with it for awhile. Had one hero keep it on the entire game as it didn't effect much at all.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That really depends on what cards they get. We had Wraith get hit with it, thinking it wouldn't be too bad, then realized it shut down Smoke Bombs and Megacomputer, and that she was no longer going to get any benefits from any other heros (such as AA's ability to let other heroes use powers or be healed).</p>\n<p>But none of the other heroes were going to be any better off, so it didn't really matter.</p>\n<p>I think Haka's Rampage and NightMist's Oblivion are two examples of where Isolated Hero is actually really nice to have around, though!  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:31:25.485Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
